WEBVTT

00:00:02.061 --> 00:00:03.469
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:06.531 --> 00:00:08.511
Take your brother outside
as fast as you  can!

00:00:08.653 --> 00:00:09.633
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:11.546 --> 00:00:12.750
Mary! No!

00:00:14.852 --> 00:00:15.873
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:18.486
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:22.010
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:23.806
I can't do this alone.

00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:27.086
No!

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:31.025
We got work to do.

00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:34.121
This is dad's single
most valuable possession

00:00:34.162 --> 00:00:36.325
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:38.407
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:38.529 --> 00:00:40.856
You know, saving people, hunting things,

00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:41.870
Family business.

00:00:41.911 --> 00:00:43.768
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:45.319
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.136
Sam, You know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:49.946
Yeah. I know.

00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:01.403
Okay, your turn. Truth or dare?

00:01:01.826 --> 00:01:02.479
Truth.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.152
Do you want to make
out with benji swartz?

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:07.091
Dare.

00:01:07.642 --> 00:01:08.806
Okay, lame.

00:01:09.718 --> 00:01:10.901
You have to...

00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:13.759
Say "bloody mary" in the bathroom.

00:01:14.426 --> 00:01:16.345
Is that the best you can come up with?

00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:17.855
Who's bloody mary?

00:01:18.365 --> 00:01:19.692
She's this witch.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.958
I heard she was a lady
killed in a car crash.

00:01:22.447 --> 00:01:23.815
It doesn't matter who she is.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.961
If you say her name three
times in the bathroom mirror,

00:01:27.777 --> 00:01:28.899
She appears...

00:01:29.593 --> 00:01:30.900
And scratches your eyes out!

00:01:33.656 --> 00:01:35.432
So why would anyone say it?

00:01:36.126 --> 00:01:37.616
Because it isn't real.

00:01:39.044 --> 00:01:40.371
No turning on the lights.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:41.949
And remember,

00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:42.949
Three times.

00:02:08.765 --> 00:02:09.704
Bloody mary.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.785
This is so stupid.

00:02:16.791 --> 00:02:17.729
Bloody mary.

00:02:28.423 --> 00:02:29.444
Bloody mary.

00:02:40.146 --> 00:02:40.799
Scared you.

00:02:40.922 --> 00:02:42.105
You guys are jerks.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.065
Lily?

00:02:43.738 --> 00:02:44.779
You mind keeping it down?

00:02:45.657 --> 00:02:46.657
Sorry, daddy.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.494
Sorry, mr. Shoemaker.

00:03:26.803 --> 00:03:28.191
You so like him!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:30.899
Hey, geek.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.491
You guys having fun?

00:03:32.818 --> 00:03:34.103
You're out past curfew.

00:03:34.812 --> 00:03:35.669
Thanks, dad.

00:04:17.611 --> 00:04:18.754
Why Sam?

00:04:20.741 --> 00:04:21.353
No!

00:04:24.735 --> 00:04:26.551
Why Sam? Sam, wake up.

00:04:35.363 --> 00:04:37.261
I take it I was having a nightmare?

00:04:38.098 --> 00:04:39.649
Yeah, another one.

00:04:43.276 --> 00:04:44.746
Hey, at least I got some sleep.

00:04:44.909 --> 00:04:47.175
Hey, you know, sooner or later,
we're gonna talk about this.

00:04:48.134 --> 00:04:48.848
Are we here?

00:04:49.256 --> 00:04:51.726
Yep. Welcome to Toledo, Ohio.

00:04:55.421 --> 00:04:57.523
So, what do you think
really happened to this guy?

00:04:57.557 --> 00:04:59.170
So what we're gonna find out.

00:05:01.721 --> 00:05:02.517
Let's go.

00:05:31.742 --> 00:05:32.253
Hey.

00:05:32.987 --> 00:05:33.600
Hey.

00:05:35.008 --> 00:05:35.763
Can I help you?

00:05:36.416 --> 00:05:38.478
Yeah, we're the... med students.

00:05:38.985 --> 00:05:39.557
Sorry?

00:05:39.924 --> 00:05:40.822
Oh, doctor...

00:05:41.455 --> 00:05:43.067
Fliglavitch didn't tell you?

00:05:43.128 --> 00:05:45.026
We talked to him on the phone.

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:46.394
We're from Ohio state.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.737
He's supposed to show
us the shoemaker corpse.

00:05:48.758 --> 00:05:49.513
It's for our paper.

00:05:49.778 --> 00:05:51.574
Well, I'm sorry, he's at lunch.

00:05:51.738 --> 00:05:52.391
Oh.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:53.615
Well, he said, uh

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.064
Oh, well, you know, it doesn't matter.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.533
You don't mind showing
us the body, do you?

00:05:57.574 --> 00:05:58.798
Sorry, I can't.

00:05:59.002 --> 00:06:01.268
Doc will be back in an
hour. You can wait for him,

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.023
If you want.

00:06:02.186 --> 00:06:02.941
An hour?

00:06:04.312 --> 00:06:06.046
We got to be heading back to columbus.

00:06:06.108 --> 00:06:06.740
Yeah.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:09.087
Look man, this paper's half our grade,

00:06:09.128 --> 00:06:10.904
So if you don't mind
helping us out? Look, man

00:06:12.159 --> 00:06:12.914
No.

00:06:15.302 --> 00:06:17.160
I'm gonna hit him in his face, I swear.

00:06:31.052 --> 00:06:32.093
Follow me.

00:06:35.985 --> 00:06:37.522
Dude, I earned that money.

00:06:37.639 --> 00:06:39.169
You won it in a poker game.

00:06:39.394 --> 00:06:40.190
Yeah.

00:06:40.904 --> 00:06:42.802
The newspaper said
his daughter found him.

00:06:43.204 --> 00:06:44.755
She said his eyes were bleeding.

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:45.898
More than that.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:47.572
They practically liquefied.

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:54.385
Any sign of a struggle,
maybe somebody did it to him?

00:06:54.566 --> 00:06:55.239
Nope.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.342
Besides the daughter, he was all alone.

00:06:58.168 --> 00:06:59.805
What's the official causeof death?

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.963
Doc's not sure. He's
thinking massive stroke,

00:07:02.987 --> 00:07:04.554
Maybe an aneurysm.

00:07:05.232 --> 00:07:06.870
Something burst up in
there, that's for sure.

00:07:07.448 --> 00:07:08.337
What do you mean?

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:10.606
Intense cerebral bleeding.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.389
This guy had more blooding his
skull than anyone I've ever seen.

00:07:14.325 --> 00:07:15.284
But the eyes?

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:17.085
What would cause something like that?

00:07:17.283 --> 00:07:18.850
Capillaries can burst.

00:07:18.897 --> 00:07:20.862
See a lot of bloodshot
eyes with stroke victims.

00:07:21.213 --> 00:07:23.341
Yeah, you ever see exploding eyeballs?

00:07:23.879 --> 00:07:25.260
That's a first for me.

00:07:25.377 --> 00:07:27.037
But, hey, I'm not the doctor.

00:07:28.538 --> 00:07:30.644
Think we could take a
look atthat police report?

00:07:30.761 --> 00:07:32.398
You know, for our paper?

00:07:33.264 --> 00:07:35.603
I'm not really supposed to show you

00:07:39.702 --> 00:07:41.199
Might not be one of ours.

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:43.257
Might just be some freak medical thing.

00:07:43.749 --> 00:07:45.198
How many times in dad's long

00:07:45.199 --> 00:07:48.333
And varied career has it actually
been a freak medical thing

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.554
And not some sign of an
awful supernatural death?

00:07:51.694 --> 00:07:53.636
Uh, almost never.

00:07:53.823 --> 00:07:54.829
Exactly.

00:07:54.946 --> 00:07:55.811
All right.

00:07:56.115 --> 00:07:57.628
Let's go talk to the daughter.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.414
Feel like we're underdressed.

00:08:26.761 --> 00:08:28.087
You must be Donna,right?

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:28.883
Yeah.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.859
Hi, uh... We're really sorry.

00:08:33.748 --> 00:08:34.520
Thank you.

00:08:35.035 --> 00:08:36.976
I'm sam.This is dean.

00:08:37.871 --> 00:08:39.134
We worked with your dad.

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:41.262
You did?

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:42.830
Yeah.This whole thing

00:08:43.625 --> 00:08:44.795
I mean, a stroke.

00:08:46.381 --> 00:08:48.322
I don't think she really wants
to talk about this right now.

00:08:48.323 --> 00:08:49.609
It's okay, I'm okay.

00:08:51.294 --> 00:08:52.674
Were there ever any symptoms?

00:08:52.791 --> 00:08:54.078
Dizziness, migraines?

00:08:55.154 --> 00:08:56.019
No.

00:08:57.233 --> 00:08:59.175
That's because it wasn't a stroke.

00:08:59.409 --> 00:09:00.415
Lily, don't say that.

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:01.374
What?

00:09:02.169 --> 00:09:03.666
I'm sorry, she's just upset.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.654
No, it happened because of me.

00:09:05.725 --> 00:09:06.988
Sweetie, it didn't.

00:09:07.069 --> 00:09:07.865
Lily,

00:09:08.866 --> 00:09:10.621
Why would you saysomething like that?

00:09:11.559 --> 00:09:13.173
Right before he died,I said it.

00:09:13.875 --> 00:09:14.694
You said what?

00:09:15.419 --> 00:09:17.922
Bloody Mary, three times
in the bathroom mirror.

00:09:21.353 --> 00:09:23.014
She took his eyes, that's what she does.

00:09:23.084 --> 00:09:25.494
That's not why dad
died.This isn't your fault.

00:09:26.219 --> 00:09:27.739
I think your sister's right,lily.

00:09:28.621 --> 00:09:30.749
There's no way it could
have been Bloody Mary.

00:09:31.896 --> 00:09:34.118
Your dad didn't say it,did he?

00:09:35.849 --> 00:09:37.322
No, I don't think so.

00:10:02.615 --> 00:10:03.972
Sam:The Bloody Mary legend

00:10:05.808 --> 00:10:08.299
Dad ever find any evidence
that it was a real thing?

00:10:09.094 --> 00:10:10.357
Not that I know of.

00:10:15.602 --> 00:10:16.397
I mean,

00:10:16.912 --> 00:10:17.988
Everywhere else,

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:23.126
All over the country,
kids will play Bloody Mary.

00:10:23.127 --> 00:10:25.373
And as far as we know,
nobody dies from it.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:27.209
Hey well, maybe everywhere
it's just a story,

00:10:27.232 --> 00:10:28.846
But here it's actually happening.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.530
The place where the legend began?

00:10:31.856 --> 00:10:34.079
But according to the legend,
the person who says...

00:10:37.166 --> 00:10:39.880
The person who says
you know what gets it

00:10:39.903 --> 00:10:40.488
But here...

00:10:40.511 --> 00:10:42.055
Shoemaker gets it instead,yeah.

00:10:42.102 --> 00:10:42.710
Right.

00:10:43.739 --> 00:10:45.540
Never heard anything like that before.

00:10:46.352 --> 00:10:48.832
Still, the guy did die
right in front of the mirror.

00:10:49.031 --> 00:10:51.229
And the daughter's right.
The way the legend goes,

00:10:51.924 --> 00:10:53.772
"You know who" scratches your eyes out.

00:10:53.936 --> 00:10:55.292
It's worth checking into.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:03.479
What are you doingup here?

00:11:04.819 --> 00:11:05.590
We...

00:11:06.175 --> 00:11:07.555
We had to go to the bathroom.

00:11:08.585 --> 00:11:09.520
Who are you?

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.076
Like we said downstairs,
we worked with Donna's dad.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.953
He was a day trader or
something, he worked by himself.

00:11:16.236 --> 00:11:17.733
No, I know, I meant...

00:11:17.896 --> 00:11:19.955
And those weird questions downstairs,

00:11:20.914 --> 00:11:21.990
What was that?

00:11:24.072 --> 00:11:25.896
So you tell me what's going on

00:11:26.508 --> 00:11:27.654
Or I start screaming.

00:11:27.888 --> 00:11:29.011
All right, all right.

00:11:31.329 --> 00:11:33.411
We think something
happened to Donna's dad.

00:11:33.528 --> 00:11:34.604
Yeah, a stroke.

00:11:34.931 --> 00:11:36.756
That's not the sign of a typical stroke.

00:11:39.142 --> 00:11:40.639
We think it might be something else.

00:11:41.364 --> 00:11:42.129
Like what?

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:43.743
Honestly,

00:11:44.936 --> 00:11:45.965
We don't know yet.

00:11:47.088 --> 00:11:49.193
But we don't want it to
happen to anyone else.

00:11:49.661 --> 00:11:50.496
That's the truth.

00:11:51.408 --> 00:11:52.063
So,

00:11:52.601 --> 00:11:53.794
If you're gonna scream,

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.736
Go right ahead.

00:11:58.332 --> 00:11:59.331
Who are you, cops?

00:12:01.857 --> 00:12:02.746
Something like that.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:03.869
I'll tell you what.

00:12:04.126 --> 00:12:04.781
Here.

00:12:05.249 --> 00:12:06.477
If you think of anything,

00:12:06.547 --> 00:12:08.489
You or your friends
notice anything strange,

00:12:08.769 --> 00:12:11.062
Out of the ordinary,
just give us a call.

00:12:19.529 --> 00:12:21.627
All right, say Bloody Mary
really is haunting this town.

00:12:21.651 --> 00:12:23.639
There's gonna be some sort of proof

00:12:23.733 --> 00:12:25.136
A local woman who died nasty.

00:12:25.276 --> 00:12:27.171
Yeah, but a legend this
wide spread, it's hard.

00:12:27.194 --> 00:12:29.532
I mean, there's like 50
versions of who she actually is.

00:12:29.533 --> 00:12:30.690
One story says she's a witch,

00:12:30.691 --> 00:12:32.866
Another says she's a mutilated bride.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.989
There's a lot more.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:35.720
What are we supposed to be looking for?

00:12:35.854 --> 00:12:37.679
Every version's got thingsin common.

00:12:37.702 --> 00:12:38.918
It's always a woman named Mary,

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:41.035
And she always dies
in front of a mirror.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:43.251
So we've got to search local newspapers

00:12:43.274 --> 00:12:45.192
Public records as far back as they go,

00:12:45.286 --> 00:12:47.157
See if we can find a
Mary who fits the bill.

00:12:47.789 --> 00:12:48.888
Well, that sounds annoying.

00:12:49.075 --> 00:12:50.689
No, it won't be so bad,

00:12:50.759 --> 00:12:51.718
As long as we...

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:54.556
I take it back.

00:12:55.234 --> 00:12:56.661
This will be very annoying.

00:12:59.702 --> 00:13:02.848
I'm not sure. They were cops
or detectives or something.

00:13:03.129 --> 00:13:05.047
Whoever they were, they were cute.

00:13:05.164 --> 00:13:05.912
Jill.

00:13:06.029 --> 00:13:06.989
You didn't think so?

00:13:07.224 --> 00:13:09.025
Yeah, okay,they were cute. But,

00:13:09.836 --> 00:13:12.760
Still,do you think something
could have happenedto Donna's dad?

00:13:12.894 --> 00:13:14.280
Maybe Lily was right.

00:13:14.882 --> 00:13:16.730
Maybe Bloody Mary got him.

00:13:17.666 --> 00:13:18.665
Very funny.

00:13:19.811 --> 00:13:21.729
Wait, I'm sorry.

00:13:22.454 --> 00:13:24.653
Was that fear I hear in your voice?

00:13:25.261 --> 00:13:26.033
No.

00:13:27.359 --> 00:13:28.178
Charlie...

00:13:28.412 --> 00:13:30.260
I'm walking to the
bathroom mirror right now.

00:13:31.149 --> 00:13:32.295
Jill, quit it.

00:13:35.003 --> 00:13:36.032
Oh, no,

00:13:36.383 --> 00:13:37.670
I can't help myself.

00:13:38.535 --> 00:13:39.822
I'm gonna say it.

00:13:40.898 --> 00:13:41.857
Bloody Mary.

00:13:42.692 --> 00:13:44.072
Bloody Mary.

00:13:45.055 --> 00:13:46.973
Bloody Mary.

00:13:49.352 --> 00:13:50.171
Jill?

00:13:55.107 --> 00:13:55.878
Jill!

00:14:00.422 --> 00:14:02.574
You're such a freak.
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:14:58.175 --> 00:14:59.321
You did it.

00:15:04.257 --> 00:15:05.695
You killed that boy.

00:15:25.741 --> 00:15:26.654
Why Sam?

00:15:31.581 --> 00:15:32.985
Why'd you let me fall asleep?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.207
'Cause I'm an awesome brother.

00:15:37.317 --> 00:15:38.790
So, what did you dream about?

00:15:39.562 --> 00:15:41.387
Lollipops and candy canes.

00:15:43.094 --> 00:15:44.170
Yeah, sure.

00:15:48.605 --> 00:15:49.774
You find anything?

00:15:50.078 --> 00:15:52.464
Oh, besides a whole new
level of frustration?

00:15:52.979 --> 00:15:55.061
No. I've looked at everything.

00:15:57.158 --> 00:15:59.615
A few local women, a
Laura and a Catherine,

00:15:59.638 --> 00:16:01.463
Committed suicide in front of a mirror,

00:16:01.884 --> 00:16:03.935
And a giant mirror fell
on a guy named dave.

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:04.918
But, uh...

00:16:06.064 --> 00:16:06.836
No Mary.

00:16:11.163 --> 00:16:12.824
Maybe we just haven't found it yet.

00:16:14.087 --> 00:16:16.192
I've also been searching
for strange deaths,

00:16:16.276 --> 00:16:17.843
In the area, you know,

00:16:18.197 --> 00:16:19.858
Eyeball bleeding, that sort of thing.

00:16:19.998 --> 00:16:21.027
There's nothing.

00:16:21.869 --> 00:16:23.834
Whatever's happening here,
maybe it just ain't Mary.

00:16:30.337 --> 00:16:31.039
Hello?

00:16:38.511 --> 00:16:41.295
And they found her
on the bathroom floor.

00:16:42.441 --> 00:16:45.435
And her-Her eyes...

00:16:46.956 --> 00:16:48.430
They were gone.

00:16:49.295 --> 00:16:50.161
I'm sorry.

00:16:52.453 --> 00:16:53.576
And she said it.

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:56.937
I heard her say it.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.152
But it couldn't be because of that.

00:17:03.534 --> 00:17:04.633
I'm insane, right?

00:17:06.545 --> 00:17:07.644
No, you're not insane.

00:17:08.673 --> 00:17:11.457
God, that makes me feel so much worse.

00:17:12.432 --> 00:17:13.227
Look...

00:17:16.549 --> 00:17:18.245
We think something's happening here,

00:17:19.485 --> 00:17:21.075
Something that can't be explained.

00:17:22.191 --> 00:17:23.244
And we're gonna stop it,

00:17:24.437 --> 00:17:25.513
But we could use your help.

00:17:44.081 --> 00:17:45.578
What did you tell Jill's mom?

00:17:45.625 --> 00:17:48.245
I just said I needed some time alone
with Jill's pictures and things.

00:17:48.278 --> 00:17:48.980
Great.

00:17:49.471 --> 00:17:50.734
I hate lying to her.

00:17:51.389 --> 00:17:52.746
This is for the greater good.

00:17:52.793 --> 00:17:53.775
Hit the lights.

00:17:58.072 --> 00:17:59.499
What are you guys looking for?

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:01.784
We'll let you know
as soon as we find it.

00:18:01.854 --> 00:18:03.164
Hey, night vision.

00:18:05.036 --> 00:18:06.696
Thanks. Perfect.

00:18:09.974 --> 00:18:11.284
Do I look like Paris Hilton?

00:18:22.969 --> 00:18:24.700
So, I don't get it.

00:18:24.724 --> 00:18:27.133
I mean, the first victim
didn't summon Mary,

00:18:27.157 --> 00:18:28.794
And the second victim did.

00:18:29.145 --> 00:18:30.431
How's she choosing them?

00:18:30.969 --> 00:18:31.695
Beats me.

00:18:36.257 --> 00:18:38.245
I want to know why Jill
said it in the first place.

00:18:39.415 --> 00:18:40.444
It's just a joke.

00:18:40.811 --> 00:18:43.688
Somebody's gonna say it again.
It's just a matter of time.

00:18:56.372 --> 00:18:57.051
Hey.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:18:59.897
There's a black light
in the trunk, right?

00:19:22.591 --> 00:19:24.299
Gary Bryman?

00:19:25.936 --> 00:19:27.163
You know who that is?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.222
No.

00:19:37.021 --> 00:19:40.202
So, Gary Bryman was an 8 year-Old boy.

00:19:41.115 --> 00:19:43.197
Two years ago, he was
killed in a hit and run.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:46.121
The car was described
as a black toyota camry,

00:19:46.722 --> 00:19:49.178
But nobody got the
plates or saw the driver.

00:19:49.506 --> 00:19:50.348
Oh, my god.

00:19:51.307 --> 00:19:51.915
What?

00:19:52.359 --> 00:19:53.763
Jill drove that car.

00:19:56.975 --> 00:19:58.729
We need to get back to
your friend Donna's house.

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:09.311
Linda shoemaker.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:14.177
Why are you asking me this?

00:20:14.539 --> 00:20:16.567
Look, we're sorry, but it's important.

00:20:17.666 --> 00:20:18.321
Yeah.

00:20:18.622 --> 00:20:19.956
Linda's my mom, okay?

00:20:20.283 --> 00:20:22.178
And she overdosed on sleeping pills.

00:20:22.295 --> 00:20:23.979
It was an accident, and that's it.

00:20:27.311 --> 00:20:28.270
I think you should leave.

00:20:28.293 --> 00:20:30.071
Donna, just listen Get out of my house!

00:20:34.392 --> 00:20:35.304
Oh, my god.

00:20:36.591 --> 00:20:39.222
Do you really think her dad
could have killed her mom?

00:20:40.603 --> 00:20:41.538
Maybe.

00:20:42.151 --> 00:20:43.531
I think I should stick around.

00:20:45.168 --> 00:20:46.805
All right. Whatever you do, don't...

00:20:46.993 --> 00:20:49.308
Believe me, I won't say it.

00:20:53.618 --> 00:20:54.811
Wait, wait, wait.

00:20:55.116 --> 00:20:57.057
You're doing a nationwide search?

00:20:57.197 --> 00:20:57.829
Yep.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.675
The NCIC, the FBI database

00:21:00.868 --> 00:21:04.084
Any mary in the country who died in
front of a mirror is good enough for me.

00:21:04.494 --> 00:21:07.464
But if she's haunting the town,
she should have died in the town.

00:21:07.623 --> 00:21:10.547
I'm telling you. There's nothing local. I
check. So, unless you've gota better idea.

00:21:10.659 --> 00:21:13.003
Why Mary's choosing a victim?
It seems like there's a pattern.

00:21:13.043 --> 00:21:14.245
I know I was thinking the same thing.

00:21:14.325 --> 00:21:16.329
With mr. Shoemaker
and Jill's hit and run

00:21:16.349 --> 00:21:17.871
Both had secrets where people died.

00:21:17.931 --> 00:21:18.432
Right.

00:21:18.512 --> 00:21:19.896
There's a lot of folklore about mirrors

00:21:19.897 --> 00:21:21.900
That they reveal or your
lies, or your secrets,

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:24.023
That they're a true
reflection of your soul,

00:21:24.024 --> 00:21:25.466
Which is why it's bad
luck to break them.

00:21:25.546 --> 00:21:26.408
Right. Right.

00:21:27.282 --> 00:21:28.644
Yeah, so maybe if you've got a secret,

00:21:28.664 --> 00:21:30.498
I mean, like a really nasty
one where someone died,

00:21:30.499 --> 00:21:32.903
Then mary sees it and
punishes you for it.

00:21:33.035 --> 00:21:34.736
Whether you summoned her or not.

00:21:35.619 --> 00:21:36.601
Take a look at this.

00:21:49.305 --> 00:21:50.908
Looks like the same handprint.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.073
Her name was Mary Worthington

00:21:53.896 --> 00:21:56.120
An unsolved murder in
Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:21:58.346 --> 00:22:01.131
I was on the job for 35 years,

00:22:01.371 --> 00:22:02.653
Detective for most of that.

00:22:03.414 --> 00:22:05.778
Now, everybody packs it
in with a few loose ends,

00:22:05.861 --> 00:22:07.784
But the Mary Worthington murder...

00:22:09.647 --> 00:22:11.030
That one still gets me.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:12.432
What exactly happened?

00:22:13.896 --> 00:22:15.619
You boys said you were reporters.

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:17.542
We know Mary was 19,

00:22:17.685 --> 00:22:18.787
Lived by herself.

00:22:18.927 --> 00:22:20.730
We know she won a few beauty contests,

00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:22.252
Dreamt of getting out of Indiana,

00:22:22.773 --> 00:22:23.715
Being an actress.

00:22:24.214 --> 00:22:26.258
And we know, the night of march 29th,

00:22:26.779 --> 00:22:28.161
Someone broke into her apartment

00:22:28.301 --> 00:22:29.143
And murdered her,

00:22:30.064 --> 00:22:31.266
Cut out her eyeswith a knife.

00:22:33.111 --> 00:22:33.872
That's right.

00:22:35.996 --> 00:22:38.240
See, sir, when we ask you what
happened, we want to know what

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:39.401
You think happened.

00:22:42.971 --> 00:22:45.956
Technically, I'm not supposed
to have a copy of this.

00:22:52.106 --> 00:22:52.707
Now,

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:55.371
See that there,

00:22:55.952 --> 00:22:56.794

"T-R-E"?

00:22:57.295 --> 00:22:57.916
Yeah.

00:22:58.647 --> 00:23:01.333
I think Mary was trying to
spell out the name of her killer.

00:23:01.414 --> 00:23:02.395
You know who it was?

00:23:02.816 --> 00:23:03.838
Not for sure.

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:06.722
But there was a local man,

00:23:06.803 --> 00:23:07.684
A surgeon,

00:23:08.247 --> 00:23:09.269
Trevor Sampson.

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:11.833
And I think he cut her up good.

00:23:12.314 --> 00:23:14.372
Now, why would he do
something like that?

00:23:14.913 --> 00:23:17.096
Her diary mentioned
a man she was seeing.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.723
She called him by his initial, "T."

00:23:20.524 --> 00:23:21.226
Well,

00:23:21.887 --> 00:23:23.590
Her last entry,

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:26.915
She was gonna tell to his
wife about their affair.

00:23:27.137 --> 00:23:29.240
But how do you know it
was Sampson who killed her?

00:23:29.862 --> 00:23:31.164
It's hard to say.

00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:36.735
But the way her eyes were cut
out, it was almost professional.

00:23:37.897 --> 00:23:39.321
But you could never prove it?

00:23:39.442 --> 00:23:39.962
No.

00:23:40.443 --> 00:23:41.265
No prints,

00:23:41.365 --> 00:23:42.547
No witnesses.

00:23:43.388 --> 00:23:44.570
He was meticulous.

00:23:46.333 --> 00:23:47.395
Is he still alive?

00:23:49.236 --> 00:23:49.817
Nope.

00:23:52.642 --> 00:23:53.743
If you ask me,

00:23:54.124 --> 00:23:57.109
Mary spent her last living moments

00:23:57.572 --> 00:23:59.876
Trying to expose this guy's secret.

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:03.222
But she never could.

00:24:05.385 --> 00:24:06.347
Where's she buried?

00:24:07.893 --> 00:24:08.695
She wasn't.

00:24:09.135 --> 00:24:09.937
She was cremated.

00:24:13.342 --> 00:24:16.027
What about that mirror?  It's not
in evidence lockup somewhere, is it?

00:24:17.847 --> 00:24:18.588
No.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.415
It was returned to Mary's
family a long time ago.

00:24:24.037 --> 00:24:26.121
You have the names of
her family by any chance?

00:24:31.391 --> 00:24:33.356
I mean, you bring these
strangers into my house,

00:24:33.376 --> 00:24:34.919
And they ask me things like that?

00:24:34.959 --> 00:24:36.261
They were only trying to help.

00:24:36.361 --> 00:24:38.425
Please, Donna, you have to believe me.

00:24:38.625 --> 00:24:40.408
What? About bloody mary?

00:24:40.650 --> 00:24:42.774
Please, I know it sounds crazy.

00:24:43.134 --> 00:24:45.057
"Crazy" doesn't even begin to cover it.

00:24:45.278 --> 00:24:47.421
I mean, it's one thing for my
sister to believe this crap.

00:24:47.523 --> 00:24:49.367
She's 12. But you?

00:24:49.889 --> 00:24:50.851
Think about the way

00:24:51.632 --> 00:24:52.553
Your dad died,

00:24:52.994 --> 00:24:55.058
Okay, and the way Jill died.

00:24:56.382 --> 00:24:57.965
Okay, so...

00:24:59.107 --> 00:24:59.667
Bloody Mary.

00:24:59.708 --> 00:25:00.068
No!

00:25:00.108 --> 00:25:02.011
Bloody Mary. Bloody Mary.

00:25:04.978 --> 00:25:06.861
See? Nothing happened.

00:25:07.322 --> 00:25:08.604
Why would you do that?

00:25:09.145 --> 00:25:10.127
Oh, my god,

00:25:10.728 --> 00:25:12.751
There really is
something wrong with you.

00:25:24.627 --> 00:25:27.572
Elements that lose electrons become

00:25:27.712 --> 00:25:29.055
Positive ions,

00:25:29.596 --> 00:25:32.701
Which are smaller than other
atoms of the same element.

00:25:33.222 --> 00:25:35.766
Therefore, the ionic radius

00:25:35.897 --> 00:25:38.201
Is smaller than the atomic radius

00:25:43.435 --> 00:25:44.276
Charlie!

00:25:49.106 --> 00:25:49.868
Charlie!

00:25:54.818 --> 00:25:57.747
Charlie, stop it! What's
wrong? Just calm down!

00:26:00.855 --> 00:26:02.134
Charlie! Aah! Let me go!

00:26:02.264 --> 00:26:03.024
Charlie!

00:26:05.323 --> 00:26:06.065
Oh, really?

00:26:06.529 --> 00:26:08.642
Ah, that's too bad, Mr. Worthington.

00:26:09.208 --> 00:26:10.951
I would have paid a lot for that mirror.

00:26:10.988 --> 00:26:12.231
Okay, well, maybe next time.

00:26:12.453 --> 00:26:13.640
All right, thanks.

00:26:13.788 --> 00:26:14.493
So?

00:26:14.697 --> 00:26:16.551
So, that was Mary's brother.

00:26:16.727 --> 00:26:19.045
The mirror was in the family for years,

00:26:19.101 --> 00:26:20.436
Until he sold it

00:26:20.695 --> 00:26:21.789
One week ago

00:26:22.883 --> 00:26:24.867
To a store called estate antiques,

00:26:25.303 --> 00:26:26.861
A store in Toledo.

00:26:28.715 --> 00:26:30.755
So wherever the mirror
goes, that's where Mary goes?

00:26:31.005 --> 00:26:33.397
Her spirit's definitely
tied up with it somehow.

00:26:33.527 --> 00:26:36.512
Isn't there an old superstition that
says mirrors can capture spirits?

00:26:37.097 --> 00:26:39.285
Yeah, there is. When
someone would die in a house,

00:26:39.322 --> 00:26:41.825
People would cover up the mirrors
so the ghost wouldn't get trapped.

00:26:42.328 --> 00:26:44.561
This Mary dies in front of the
mirror, and it draws in her spirit.

00:26:44.850 --> 00:26:47.835
Yeah, but how could she move
through 100 different mirrors?

00:26:48.484 --> 00:26:50.014
I don't know but if the
mirror is the source,

00:26:50.033 --> 00:26:51.572
I say we find it and smash it.

00:26:52.925 --> 00:26:54.464
Yeah, I don't know. Maybe.

00:26:58.678 --> 00:26:59.327
Hello?

00:27:00.773 --> 00:27:01.496
Charlie?

00:27:20.557 --> 00:27:21.298
Hey.

00:27:22.244 --> 00:27:23.264
Hey. It's okay.

00:27:24.061 --> 00:27:25.767
You can open up your eyes, Charlie.

00:27:25.814 --> 00:27:27.575
It's okay, all right?

00:27:28.929 --> 00:27:29.745
Now, listen.

00:27:30.431 --> 00:27:31.729
You're gonna stay right here

00:27:32.331 --> 00:27:33.129
On this bed.

00:27:33.731 --> 00:27:35.178
You're not gonna look at glass

00:27:35.345 --> 00:27:37.347
Or anything else that
has a reflection, okay?

00:27:38.155 --> 00:27:39.341
As long as you do that

00:27:40.157 --> 00:27:41.585
She cannot get you.

00:27:44.691 --> 00:27:46.471
But I can't keep that up forever.

00:27:49.314 --> 00:27:50.798
I'm gonna die, aren't I?

00:27:52.707 --> 00:27:53.301
No.

00:27:54.895 --> 00:27:55.581
No.

00:27:57.371 --> 00:27:58.548
Not anytime soon.

00:28:00.746 --> 00:28:01.784
All right, Charlie,

00:28:02.470 --> 00:28:03.527
We need to know what happened.

00:28:04.510 --> 00:28:05.826
We were in the bathroom.

00:28:06.077 --> 00:28:06.967
Donna said it.

00:28:07.004 --> 00:28:08.561
That's not what we're talking about.

00:28:12.029 --> 00:28:13.586
Something happened, didn't it,

00:28:15.014 --> 00:28:16.015
In your life.

00:28:17.867 --> 00:28:18.645
A secret...

00:28:19.906 --> 00:28:21.140
Where someone got hurt?

00:28:27.110 --> 00:28:28.436
Can you tell us about it?

00:28:32.553 --> 00:28:33.721
I had this boyfriend.

00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:37.570
I loved him.

00:28:39.387 --> 00:28:41.681
But he kind of scared me, too, you know?

00:28:42.690 --> 00:28:43.560
And...

00:28:43.815 --> 00:28:44.729
One night

00:28:45.281 --> 00:28:46.428
At his house,

00:28:46.746 --> 00:28:47.893
We got in this fight.

00:28:50.293 --> 00:28:51.716
Then I broke up with him,

00:28:52.905 --> 00:28:55.093
And he got upset and he said

00:28:55.369 --> 00:28:57.726
He needed me and he loved me.

00:28:59.224 --> 00:29:00.179
And he said...

00:29:01.220 --> 00:29:04.130
"Charlie, if you walk out that door
right now, I'm gonna kill myself."

00:29:06.997 --> 00:29:08.441
And you know what I said?

00:29:10.061 --> 00:29:11.335
I said, "go ahead."

00:29:14.351 --> 00:29:15.562
And I left.

00:29:18.769 --> 00:29:20.107
How could I say that?

00:29:25.406 --> 00:29:27.254
How could I leave him like that?

00:29:30.340 --> 00:29:31.444
I just...

00:29:32.230 --> 00:29:34.142
I didn't believe him, you know?

00:29:41.043 --> 00:29:42.211
I should have.

00:29:51.336 --> 00:29:54.331
Her boyfriend killing himself,
that's not really Charlie's fault.

00:29:55.244 --> 00:29:56.369
You know as well as I do,

00:29:56.391 --> 00:29:59.131
Spirits don't exactly
see shades of gray,

00:29:59.194 --> 00:29:59.980
Dean.

00:30:00.373 --> 00:30:01.541
Charlie had a secret,

00:30:01.838 --> 00:30:02.815
Someone died.

00:30:03.367 --> 00:30:04.514
That's good enough for Mary.

00:30:05.321 --> 00:30:06.298
I guess.

00:30:06.957 --> 00:30:08.167
You know,I've been thinking,

00:30:09.112 --> 00:30:11.809
It might not be enough
to just smash that mirror.

00:30:12.404 --> 00:30:13.466
Why, what do you mean?

00:30:13.742 --> 00:30:15.059
Mary's hard to pin down, right?

00:30:15.123 --> 00:30:16.822
And she moves around
from mirror to mirror.

00:30:16.843 --> 00:30:19.829
So, who's to say that she's not gonna
just keep hiding in them forever?

00:30:21.252 --> 00:30:22.441
So maybe...

00:30:23.737 --> 00:30:25.245
We should try to pin her down,

00:30:26.356 --> 00:30:28.565
You know, summon her to her mirror

00:30:29.415 --> 00:30:30.604
And then smash it.

00:30:31.241 --> 00:30:32.622
Well, how do you know that's gonna work?

00:30:32.686 --> 00:30:33.471
I don't,

00:30:34.172 --> 00:30:35.383
I'm not for sure.

00:30:37.993 --> 00:30:39.352
Well, who's gonnasummon her?

00:30:41.157 --> 00:30:41.901
I will.

00:30:44.046 --> 00:30:45.299
She'll come after me.

00:30:47.242 --> 00:30:49.111
All right, you know what? That's it.

00:30:59.349 --> 00:31:00.730
This is about Jessica, isn't it?

00:31:04.935 --> 00:31:06.252
You think that's your
dirty little secret,

00:31:06.273 --> 00:31:08.100
That you killed her somehow?

00:31:11.345 --> 00:31:13.511
Sam, this has got to stop, man.

00:31:15.146 --> 00:31:15.953
I mean,

00:31:16.315 --> 00:31:17.674
The nightmares and-And

00:31:17.790 --> 00:31:19.808
Calling her name out in
the middle of the night,

00:31:20.615 --> 00:31:21.974
It's gonna kill you.

00:31:23.291 --> 00:31:24.353
Now, listen to me.

00:31:25.755 --> 00:31:27.241
It wasn't your fault.

00:31:28.715 --> 00:31:31.519
If you want to blame something,
then blame the thing that killed her.

00:31:31.986 --> 00:31:33.473
Or, hell, why don't
you take a swing at me?

00:31:33.515 --> 00:31:36.000
I'm the one that dragged you
away from her the first place.

00:31:36.213 --> 00:31:37.360
I don't blame you.

00:31:37.905 --> 00:31:39.200
You shouldn't blame yourself,

00:31:39.625 --> 00:31:41.260
Because there's
nothingyou could've done.

00:31:41.409 --> 00:31:43.108
I could've warned her. About what?!

00:31:43.899 --> 00:31:45.556
You didn't know what was gonna happen.

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:48.104
And, besides,

00:31:48.274 --> 00:31:50.366
All of this isn't a secret.
I mean, I know all about it.

00:31:50.377 --> 00:31:51.906
It's not gonna work with Mary anyway.

00:31:52.235 --> 00:31:53.234
No, you don't.

00:31:54.720 --> 00:31:55.294
I don't what?

00:31:55.379 --> 00:31:57.630
You don't know all about it.

00:31:58.352 --> 00:31:59.775
I haven't told you everything.

00:32:01.943 --> 00:32:03.005
What are you talking about?

00:32:03.833 --> 00:32:05.978
It wouldn't really be a
secret if I told you, would it?

00:32:13.207 --> 00:32:13.950
No.

00:32:15.373 --> 00:32:16.414
I don't like it.

00:32:16.435 --> 00:32:17.986
It's not gonna happen. Forget it.

00:32:18.708 --> 00:32:20.917
Dean, that girl back
there is going to die

00:32:21.972 --> 00:32:23.777
Unless we do something about it.

00:32:24.563 --> 00:32:25.349
And you know what?

00:32:25.731 --> 00:32:28.641
Who knows how many more people
are gonna die after that?

00:32:30.107 --> 00:32:31.190
Now, we're doing this.

00:32:34.025 --> 00:32:36.213
You've got to let me do this.

00:33:03.813 --> 00:33:06.043
Well, that's just great.

00:33:15.834 --> 00:33:17.427
All right, let's start looking.

00:33:56.250 --> 00:33:57.822
Maybe they've already sold it.

00:34:03.525 --> 00:34:04.672
I don't think so.

00:34:17.304 --> 00:34:18.303
That's it.

00:34:21.361 --> 00:34:22.572
You sure about this?

00:34:39.467 --> 00:34:40.444
Bloody Mary.

00:34:43.545 --> 00:34:44.607
Bloody Mary.

00:34:56.223 --> 00:34:57.052
Bloody Mary.

00:35:07.360 --> 00:35:09.251
I'll go check that out.
Stay here. Be careful.

00:35:11.618 --> 00:35:13.254
Smash anything that moves.

00:35:24.610 --> 00:35:25.502
Crap.

00:35:44.036 --> 00:35:44.991
Hold on

00:35:45.246 --> 00:35:47.816
Whoa, guys, false alarm.

00:35:48.326 --> 00:35:49.473
I tripped the system.

00:35:49.590 --> 00:35:50.482
Who are you?

00:35:51.161 --> 00:35:52.266
I'm the boss's kid.

00:35:54.007 --> 00:35:55.452
You're Mr. Yamashiro's kid?

00:36:11.116 --> 00:36:12.199
Come on.

00:36:13.324 --> 00:36:14.535
Come into this one.

00:36:38.270 --> 00:36:39.321
It's your fault.

00:36:40.766 --> 00:36:41.849
You killed her.

00:36:45.566 --> 00:36:46.861
You killed Jessica.

00:36:50.492 --> 00:36:52.297
Like I said, I was adopted.

00:36:53.072 --> 00:36:53.858
Yeah.

00:36:56.577 --> 00:36:57.596
You know, I just

00:36:58.287 --> 00:37:00.432
I really don't have
timefor this right now.

00:37:06.485 --> 00:37:07.823
You never told her the truth,

00:37:08.513 --> 00:37:09.724
Who you really were.

00:37:10.467 --> 00:37:12.166
But it's more than that,isn't it?

00:37:13.122 --> 00:37:14.715
Those nightmares you've been having

00:37:15.150 --> 00:37:16.658
Of jessica dying,

00:37:17.104 --> 00:37:18.060
Screaming,

00:37:18.952 --> 00:37:19.823
Burning

00:37:20.524 --> 00:37:22.796
You had them for days before she died.

00:37:23.784 --> 00:37:24.804
Didn't you?!

00:37:27.352 --> 00:37:29.264
You were so desperateto ignore them,

00:37:29.285 --> 00:37:31.006
To believethey were just dreams.

00:37:31.664 --> 00:37:33.140
How could you ignore them like that?

00:37:33.777 --> 00:37:36.283
How could you leave her alone to die?

00:37:39.129 --> 00:37:40.786
You dreamt it would happen!

00:37:47.478 --> 00:37:48.264
Dude.

00:37:48.837 --> 00:37:50.281
Sammy, sammy!

00:37:52.161 --> 00:37:53.053
It's sam.

00:37:54.845 --> 00:37:56.035
God, are you okay?

00:37:56.226 --> 00:37:57.118
Uh, yeah.

00:37:59.157 --> 00:38:00.049
Come on, come on.

00:39:03.127 --> 00:39:05.272
You killed them!

00:39:05.718 --> 00:39:07.418
All those people!

00:39:07.803 --> 00:39:09.991
You killed them!

00:39:38.510 --> 00:39:39.402
Hey, sam?

00:39:40.332 --> 00:39:41.118
Yeah?

00:39:42.530 --> 00:39:45.674
That's got to be like
what, 600 years of bad luck?

00:40:10.039 --> 00:40:11.377
So this is really over?

00:40:13.227 --> 00:40:14.268
Yeah, it's over.

00:40:16.498 --> 00:40:17.348
Thank you.

00:40:29.261 --> 00:40:30.110
Charlie?

00:40:34.144 --> 00:40:35.546
Your boyfriend's death,

00:40:36.799 --> 00:40:38.561
You really should try
to forgive yourself.

00:40:39.326 --> 00:40:40.367
No matter what you did,

00:40:40.834 --> 00:40:42.066
You probably couldn't have stopped it.

00:40:44.561 --> 00:40:46.091
Sometimes bad things just happen.

00:40:57.775 --> 00:40:58.742
That's good advice.

00:41:15.272 --> 00:41:16.101
Hey, sam?

00:41:17.163 --> 00:41:17.800
Yeah?

00:41:18.788 --> 00:41:20.359
Now that this is all over,

00:41:21.336 --> 00:41:23.078
I want you to tell me
what that secret is.

00:41:28.016 --> 00:41:28.950
Look...

00:41:30.469 --> 00:41:31.467
You're my brother.

00:41:32.848 --> 00:41:34.165
And I'd die for you.

00:41:36.830 --> 00:41:38.869
But there are some things
I need to keep to myself.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
